Hola familia

I have officially been here a week, which means I am no longer the newest
one in the house (welcome to Hermana Ejemplo, who got in yesterday). It has
been a good week and a lot has happened.

The district and the house are both good and everyone is easy to be around.
My companion got called as district leader, which makes me a house leader,
which mostly means being dragged along to his meetings. There are
twenty-five of us in six rooms and something happens every night. This week
somebody took our shower door off its hinges, so we put his bed on the
roof. Nobody takes any of it personally.

Spanish is coming along. I have already passed everything I learned in two
years of classes at school. During gym we play futsal, which is soccer on a
court inside a cage. I found out this week that the president I am going to
is strict about phones, so if the photo album stops updating for a while
that is why.

On Tuesday I had to go back to the airport because there was a problem with
my documents. I missed language class, which is actually the fun part, but
I got to see a lot of M=C3=A9xico and practice with the officers at the cou=
nter.
I saw the temple too, and went back again with my district today.

I think for each of these I will do a word of the week and a verse of the
week, so the letters have a little structure.

Word of the week:
cohete -- rocket, firework

Verse of the week:
Alma 17:22-23
Ammon asked to stay among the people he had been sent to, for a time, and
perhaps until the day he died.

I miss everyone and I read all of the emails. Please write. I cannot always
answer during the week; the latest I get back to people is on Pday.=C2=A0

Hasta luego
Elder Example

Also happy birthday to Grandpa

Google Photos:
https://photos.app.goo.gl/ExampleAlbum1234

